## 149: six separately named membership tests

Since a^2+b^2=r^2, the squared norms at B(-a,b), C(-a,-b), D(a,-b),
E(b,a), K(-b,a), M(-b,-a) all equal a^2+b^2. Therefore all six lie
on the circle. Sign changes and coordinate swaps preserve the sum of squares;
this also covers coincident points and r=0 without an extra assumption.
Six independent answer labels B,C,D,E,K,M are needed if graded automatically.
The requested yes/no tests may be auto; a symmetry explanation aids display.

