## 160: a common point of all three graphs

The first line is 3x-2y=6. Together with x+y=7 it forces (4,3).
The remaining polynomial there is 16+12-18-4+3=9, not 5.
Therefore no point is common to ALL THREE graphs. Pairwise intersections
would not establish the requested common point. This is a deterministic
membership/consistency question, not a requested drawing; boolean auto is fine.

